{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552792-a-voyage-into-medieval-africa","id":1552792,"title":"A Voyage into Medieval Africa...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-01T03:21:47-07:00","id":1552792,"title":"A Voyage into Medieval Africa...","content":"Medieval Africa is a fascinating place, yet one which was barely investigated within Vampire: the Dark Ages. I thought it was about time to do something about that:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"140\" height=\"181\" data-align=\"left\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/531475-thumb140.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/531475-thumb140.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/531475-thumb140.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_left js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <b>Strongholds of the Faith</b><br /> <br /> For a thousand years the Christian lords of Nubia have stood firm against their enemies. In their cities on the banks of the Nile they have built a unique Afro-Byzantine culture, aided by their hidden protectors amongst the undead. Now, in the era of the Crusades, the people of Nubia face new challenges, and are faced with a struggle for survival against their enemies. There are those who gaze upon Nubia, and whose dark ambitions would bring ruin to these kingdoms, and all those who dwell within their borders.<br /> <br /> <b>The Kingdoms of the Nile</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Ethiopians</i> is a location sourcebook for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i>, focusing on the Afro-Byzantine kingdom of Nubia and the surrounding region. This includes Tungul, capital of Dotawo, and the most powerful city in Tungul, and Axum, the ruined centre of a fallen empire. <i>The Ethiopians</i> presents information on the culture, and geography of these locations and the surrounding region, and the dramatic histories which have affected its population, both mortal and Laibon.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ethiopians includes:</b><ul><li>Information on the history, geography, and culture of the Afro-Byzantine kingdoms of the medieval era.</li> <li>Profiles of 30 characters, with detailed information on the Laibon who reside in some of the key domains in this region.</li> <li>Maps, timelines, and other reference material designed to support chronicles set in the Afro-Byzantine kingdoms of Africa during the medieval period.</li> <li>An appendix providing information on the Laibon, designed to help both players and Storytellers experience Africa in the medieval era.</li> </ul><br /> So, it's a book about the medieval Africa, looking at some of the important kingdoms on the Nile. But wait:<br /> <br /> <b><img width=\"140\" height=\"181\" data-align=\"left\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/531476-thumb140.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/531476-thumb140.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/531476-thumb140.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_left js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> The Nile Will Run Red with Blood</b><br /> <br /> Far from the Mediterranean the Chwezi rulers of Kitara oversee a kingdom which dominates the region around Lake Nalubaale and the headwaters of the Nile. Yet the Kings of Kitara are not the true lords of their domain; in the African night there lurks predators who take on the form of men, immortal monsters who hold the power to manipulate the weak-minded fools who see themselves as kings.<br /> <br /> <b>A Journey into the Heart of Africa</b><br /> <br /> <i>The House of Set</i> is a location sourcebook for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i>, focusing on the key Laibon domains of the Kingdom of Kitara. Most notable of these is the House of Set, a Founding Temple, built to help project the power of the Setites into the heart of Africa. The book provides an exploration of the history and culture of this part of Central Africa, and examines its turbulent history, and the ongoing conflicts which threaten the Laibon of this region.<br /> <br /> <b>The House of Set includes:</b><ul><li>An exploration of the medieval Kingdom of Kitara, and the infamous Setite temple that exists hidden within this state.</li> <li>Profiles of 25 characters, representing some of the most important Laibon who dwell both in Kitara, and on the plains which lie to north of the kingdom.</li> <li>Maps, timelines, and other reference material designed to support chronicles set at the East African interior.</li> <li>An appendix providing information on the Laibon, designed to help both players and Storytellers experience Africa in the medieval era.</li> </ul>\u200bSo, actually two books on medieval Africa, because one was not quite enough. And, for anyone who wants both, there is a bundle, all available on the Storytellers Vault:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","user":"The Gentleman Gamer","date":".  No links to non-Onyx Path books, please. 08-03-2025, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T01:11:08-07:00","id":1552824,"title":"","content":"And purchased! Anything from James is buy-on-sight for me, and I'm someone who rarely buys any 3rd party content. <b>England Will Burn</b> is still one of my favorite books for VtDA, and I'm really enjoying my read through of <b>A Guide to the Night</b>.<br /> <br /> Much like <b>The Gates of Damascus</b> and <b>The Song of the Aegean</b>, these two books seem quite unique, covering geographic areas that have been generally ignored by VtDA, DA:V or VtM (the closest being <b>Cairo by Night</b>, perhaps?). Of the two, I'm most looking forward to <b>The House of Set</b>, but <b>The Ethiopians</b> may surprise me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27237-snikabar","name":"Snikabar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T13:26:15-07:00","id":1552839,"title":"","content":"Ahhh, another book for podcast! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T15:21:40-07:00","id":1552841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552792-a-voyage-into-medieval-africa?p=1552839#post1552839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahhh, another book for podcast! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Two </i>books. You get the explanation for Ignatios in <i>Song of the Aegean</i> amongst other content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}